            "accordion_row_GpGfEt": {
              "type": "_accordion-row",
              "name": "t:names.accordion_row",
              "settings": {
                "heading": "HOW SHOULD I CARE FOR MY LEATHER PRODUCT TO ENSURE IT LASTS A LONG TIME?",
                "open_by_default": false,
                "icon": "leather",
                "width": 20
              },
              "blocks": {
                "text_xkKGPc": {
                  "type": "text",
                  "name": "t:names.text",
                  "settings": {
                    "text": "<p>To maintain the beauty and longevity of your leather goods, we recommend the following:</p><ul><li><strong>Regular cleaning:</strong> Wipe your leather product with a soft, dry cloth to remove dust and dirt. Avoid using water or soap, as these can damage the leather.</li><li><strong>Conditioning:</strong> Use a high-quality leather conditioner every 6-12 months to keep the leather soft and prevent it from drying out or cracking. Apply the conditioner with a soft cloth, following the product instructions.</li><li><strong>Storage:</strong> Store your leather items in a cool, dry place away from direct sunlight, which can cause the color to fade. Use a dust bag to protect the leather from dust and scratches.</li><li><strong>Avoid moisture:</strong> Keep your leather goods away from water. If they do get wet, blot the excess water with a dry cloth and allow them to air dry naturally, away from heat sources.</li><li><strong>Handling:</strong> When handling leather products, make sure your hands are clean and dry. Oils and dirt from your hands can stain the leather over time.</li></ul>",
                    "width": "100%",
                    "max_width": "none",
                    "alignment": "left",
                    "type_preset": "custom",
                    "font": "var(--font-body--family)",
